From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:34:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dovi_ccm: the MMR mapping of the chroma with a table per
 axis, as an option

The chroma pass of the composer of ETSI GS CCM 001 (libplacebo-9930)
evaluates the 22 terms of an MMR mapping of order 3 for every chroma
sample and component, exactly (dovi_ccm.c). Ten of them depend on one of
the three samples alone: the constant, and s, s^2 and s^3 of the
down-sampled luma, of Cb and of Cr.

With pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_mmr_table, those are summed on the CPU for
every code of their sample (pl_dovi_ccm_mmr_table()), split as the shader
sums every term: the low 32 bits of the q part, the two sums of the r part
(integers below 2^19), and the float estimate made in doubles. The table is
a texture of 32-bit unsigned integers, a row for each component, piece and
axis, uploaded when the composing metadata change. The shader reads three
entries of it a component and evaluates only the twelve terms of two or
three samples, with the same expressions as before. Its sums are the same:
X modulo 2^32 in any grouping, the same integers in rh and rl, and an
estimate within the bound that dovi_ccm_prepare() checks, so the same v.
Without a sampleable RGBA32UI format (libplacebo-9976 gives the OpenGL
backend one), or where the table cannot be made, every term is evaluated
as before, and that is logged once a stream. The
chroma pass is named "DV composer: chroma (CCM 001 5.4, MMR table)" then,
so that the GPU time of each pass tells the two apart.

Whether it is faster depends on the GPU: three reads of a texture against
products and sums. It is off by default, an option for that measurement.

Measured on Mesa's zink (14 pictures of a profile 7 FEL stream, whose
chroma is MMR of order 3; fidbench in the source transport at step-down
levels 0 and 2, the converted transport, with GUI elements, and
libplacebo's reshaping; the render test with the composer and with the
reshaping): with the table, every file the same bytes as without it, and
without it the same as before this. A mutation of the table (one step of v
added on one axis) changes them.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, that of libplacebo and of the files changed,
whose notices stay as they are.
