+// Hades: the MMR mappings of the chroma with a table per axis
+// (pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_mmr_table). For chroma component ci, piece i and
+// axis a (0: the down-sampled luma s0, 1: Cb, 2: Cr), row (ci * 8 + i) * 3 + a
+// holds, for every code s of the base layer (column s, 2^BL_bit_depth of them),
+// the terms of the mapping that depend on that sample alone, C'_k tt[k] for tt
+// the sample, its square and its cube as the shader makes them (and, on axis
+// 0, the constant), summed as the shader sums every term: q, the low 32 bits
+// of the sum of floor(C'_k / 2^7) tt[k]; the sums of r_k (tt[k] >> 10) and of
+// r_k (tt[k] & 1023), exact integers below 2^19, as floats; and the float
+// estimate, the sum of f_k tt[k] made in doubles. The three floats are held as
+// their bits. `out` has PL_DOVI_CCM_MMRT_ROWS rows of 2^BL_bit_depth texels of
+// four uint32_t; the rows of a piece that is not an MMR one are zeros.
+#define PL_DOVI_CCM_MMRT_ROWS 48
+void pl_dovi_ccm_mmr_table(const struct pl_dovi_ccm_prep *pp, uint32_t *out);
